# Intent: Limiter and heap round after bench window 11. The limiter assumes the cable is in (limited) until the first real reading, a cable going in is believed at once and going out after 2 seconds. The servo layer keeps the highest speed written to each servo since the last read and the limiter status reports it (peak_dps, whole degrees per second, reset on read). self.bench.say_test plays its reply in 60 ms slices like a real reply (one long block held the speaker write and showed as slow_out lines). New build kind heap: a bench image that traces live allocations from boot, printed by self.bench.heap_trace.
# Placement: unit
# Upstream: firmware/main/hal and stackchan/motion (ours)
# Check after a flash: at boot self.motion.status reads usb_limited until the first cable reading, then follows the cable at once; after a dance self.motion.status peak_dps stays at or under the ceiling (240 limited, 400 free); say_test shows no slow_out lines.
# Kconfig: none new (the heap kind sets CONFIG_HEAP_TRACING_STANDALONE in firmware/configs/sdkconfig.heaptrace.defaults)

